WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.080
Uh, my name is Suaad Alshleh. I am a
student at the Royal College of Surgeons in Ireland and i'm 18 years old.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.880
When President von der Leyen mentioned me in her speech, 
I was incredibly surprised 

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:17.200
but also very honoured and grateful, you know, 
to be mentioned by the most powerful person in Europe.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:27.360
And we will make sure that people who have the right to stay are integrated and made to feel welcome.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:32.280
They have a future to build and skills, energy and talent. 

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:41.880
I think of Suaad, the teenage Syrian refugee who arrived in Europe dreaming of being a medical doctor.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:51.280
Within 3 years, she was awarded a prestigious scholarship 
from the Royal College of Surgeons in Ireland.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.280
I’ve always wanted to be a doctor.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:58.640
I suppose because the idea of being able to help others 
when they’re most vulnerable, that appeals to me a lot,

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.240
along with the science and the knowledge 
behind being a doctor.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.280
I could check the first line and I could see that I had an offer to RCSI 
and I genuinely started jumping up and down.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:18.880
And I called my parents, called them to come over, and it was, you know, 
that one moment where you feel like everything you’ve worked hard for has paid off.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:26.640
And I genuinely, you know my heart couldn’t stop beating 
and I was just so happy.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:31.920
So, yeah, that was probably 
my happiest moment so far in Ireland.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.560
When I first came to Ireland, 
obviously it was a period of great change for me.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.250
Everything from the simple things, 
like the weather, was different.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:49.420
But I met a lot of people that made Ireland feel like home, 
be it my friends from the schools I went to and even my friends at College now.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:54.160
So I can safely say Ireland is my home 
and I am used to the weather, crazy as it may be.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.000
Yeah, I’m really happy to be here.

